            <div xml:id="d581">

                <pb facs="0729" n="605" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg605"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2252: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Warren</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-27T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 27,
                                1921—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>165. Embassy’s no. 315, September 24, 4 p.m. Cable from Stevens states that he is
                    reliably informed that negotiations are now being carried on by Japanese to
                    purchase or lease Ussuri Railway, the negotiations <pb facs="0730" n="606"
                        xml:id="pg606"/> taking place through the channel of the South Manchuria
                    Railway.</p>
                <p>Take up as outlined our no. 158, September 21, 5 p.m., with the Japanese Foreign
                    Office.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
